label: Soil Query
description: >-
  The parcel boundary rendered as WKT, ready to be embedded in the SQL that
  goes to USDA's Soil Data Access.

  NOTE WHAT THIS EDGE IS: the point where declared structure becomes an
  untyped string again, because the wire to SDA is a SQL string and nothing
  can change that. blue-ribbon builds this in `ringToWkt`
  (apps/etl/src/fetch/ssurgo.ts:30). Making it an edge means the
  serialization is a gated, testable node instead of a helper, and it means
  the structure->string boundary is VISIBLE rather than incidental.
fields:
  pin:
    classification: linkable
    type: utf8
    label: PIN
    description: The parcel being queried
    nullable: false
    validations:
      minLength: 8
      maxLength: 40
  wkt:
    type: utf8
    label: WKT
    description: >-
      POLYGON((lng lat,...)) in EPSG:4326. Escaped and interpolated into SDA's
      SQL by the effect handler -- blue-ribbon does `parcelWkt.replace(/'/g,
      "''")` at ssurgo.ts:42 and this edge is where that obligation lives.
    nullable: false
    validations:
      minLength: 20
      maxLength: 1000000
